<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Razor">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>BotNexus.Extensions.Channels.SignalR.BlazorClient</RootNamespace>
    <Description>Shared services, contracts, and state models for the BotNexus SignalR Blazor clients.</Description>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.SignalR.Client" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- #2305 (epic #2300): the client consumes the SINGLE canonical declaration of
         ConversationKind / ConversationSource instead of hand-mirroring the wire enums. A
         duplicated enum is a contract that can silently drift: a value added server-side would
         not fail any client build, it would quietly degrade to the tolerant-parse fallback and
         render wrong.

         WASM PAYLOAD NOTE (#2329): this project feeds a Microsoft.NET.Sdk.BlazorWebAssembly app,
         so every assembly reachable from here is DOWNLOADED BY THE BROWSER. It therefore
         references BotNexus.Domain.Wire (dependency-free enums only) and deliberately NOT
         BotNexus.Domain, which pulls Vogen.SharedTypes into the payload at runtime. Do not add
         references here without checking what they drag in transitively. -->
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\domain\BotNexus.Domain.Wire\BotNexus.Domain.Wire.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- #2305 (epic #2300): the conversation-origin enums have a SINGLE canonical declaration in
         BotNexus.Gateway.Abstractions.Models; the client no longer re-declares them. Imported as
         type ALIASES rather than a whole-namespace using so unrelated same-named types in that
         namespace (e.g. SubAgentInfo) do not collide with the client's own models. -->
    <Using Include="BotNexus.Gateway.Abstractions.Models.ConversationSource" Alias="ConversationSource" />
    <Using Include="BotNexus.Gateway.Abstractions.Models.ConversationKind" Alias="ConversationKind" />
    <Using Include="BotNexus.Gateway.Abstractions.Models.ConversationVisibility" Alias="ConversationVisibility" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="BotNexus.Extensions.Channels.SignalR.BlazorClient.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- #2322 / #2334: ask_user prompt reconciliation (AskUserPromptNormalizer) is shared by every
       channel, and this client consumes it from BotNexus.Domain.Wire - referenced above - NOT from
       BotNexus.Domain.

       An earlier revision of this PR added a BotNexus.Domain ProjectReference here, justified as
       "only a Vogen source-generator package reference, so it does not weigh down the WASM
       payload". That justification was wrong, and BotNexus.Domain.csproj says so explicitly:
       PrivateAssets="all" on Vogen was TRIED and EMPIRICALLY REJECTED there, because
       Vogen.ValueObjectValidationException is a real runtime type caught by CitizenId.TryParse.
       Vogen therefore flows as a RUNTIME asset and Vogen.SharedTypes.dll lands in the browser
       download - which WasmPayloadDependencyArchitectureTests correctly failed on.

       The fix is the one #2329 proposal 3 prescribes and the fence's own allowlist comment
       demands: the shared ask_user wire shapes (AskUserPrompt, AskUserPromptChoice,
       AskUserPromptNormalizer, AskUserPromptTextRenderer) live in the zero-dependency
       BotNexus.Domain.Wire assembly, addressing conversations by plain string. The gateway maps
       those strings to and from the typed Vogen ConversationId on the SERVER via
       AskUserPromptProjection, which stays in BotNexus.Domain. Do NOT re-add a BotNexus.Domain
       reference here, and do NOT allowlist it in the fence. -->

</Project>
